WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:12.480
I know as I mentioned to you earlier how I expressed my feelings on how . . . on what the move itself did to me and affected me.

2
00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:19.980
And I wrote an open letter and I posted it on Facebook and I just have it entitled, Dear Mossville.

3
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:23.500
“For me this move has been very hard.

4
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:27.200
I married Rich in 1969.

5
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:32.660
We moved to Mossville on October 31st, 1970, Halloween.

6
00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:42.400
We built our home in 1973.So from 1973 to 2016, Prater Road was home.

7
00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:46.720
Rich, a Mossville native, passed on in 2010.

8
00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:50.900
So leaving Mossville has been like leaving him all over again.

9
00:00:50.900 --> 00:01:04.060
The move began in disbelief, then to tears, and then to a feeling of being pressured as I observed the dismantling of my community.

10
00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:13.900
My neighbors began to move; first, those to the right; then, those across the street; and last, those to the left.

11
00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:17.300
We are one of the last families to leave.

12
00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:23.240
Prater Road and Mossville will always be a part of who we are.

13
00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:26.900
My prayers for Mossville.

14
00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:35.140
My prayers for peace, joy, and security go out for all my friends who remain.

15
00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:39.360
May God continue to bless and keep you, Dear Mossville.”
